/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Functions: db, mutation, code, deferred, createBody, create, current, edit, apply, request
 *   Constants: actor, other, user, album, artist, first, second, albumTitle, provider
 *   Variables: harness, server, base, token, userToken
 * Tests
 *   - private routing rejects anonymous, ordinary users and mismatched viewer before body; current admin reads shared reviews
 *   - source snapshot retains actual names and missing naming evidence; create receipt replays across source changes
 *   - zero-track Album supports metadata-only review; malformed, excessive, mixed Video and unavailable membership fail closed
 *   - review projects never enter legacy import inventory/read/mutations/asset/duplicate/publication protocols
 *   - source status distinguishes changed metadata and unavailable lifecycle and prevents apply without blocking private draft repair
 *   - legacy file replacement without metadata revision change invalidates filename evidence and apply
 *   - manual edit and provider checkpoint preserve baseline conflict; individual adoption changes only private saved values
 *   - explicit selected apply preserves unrelated metadata, Credits, assets, visibility and membership; receipt and order commit together
 *   - concurrent private edits have one winner; concurrent application from separate projects cannot overwrite the first
 *   - late apply transaction failure rolls back prior Track updates, Album ordering and the review receipt
 *   - review/import share account admission and daily provider budgets; stopped in-flight work still occupies its slot
 *   - ambiguous provider outcome persists and blocks paid replay but allows explicit manual apply
 *   - permission loss and expired analysis grants prevent new provider calls and catalog writes
 *   - separate review inventory supports scoped pagination/counts and terminal applied filtering
 * @end-catalog */

